WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:04.004
♪♪

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:06.506
We don't really
think about it,

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:09.843
it's just always there...

00:00:11.136 --> 00:00:12.387
while astronauts are fine

00:00:12.387 --> 00:00:13.513
tuned living without it.

00:00:13.639 --> 00:00:15.140
If we're going
to inhabit space

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:16.642
for longer periods of time,

00:00:16.642 --> 00:00:18.393
it would be nice
to bring it with us.

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:25.484
Can we create
our own gravity?

00:00:26.652 --> 00:00:28.445
I'm Wrenn Schmidt
and we're exploring the

00:00:28.445 --> 00:00:30.572
science behind
"For All Mankind."

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:33.700
♪♪

00:00:37.788 --> 00:00:40.374
We wanted to kick off this
season with an event

00:00:40.374 --> 00:00:41.541
that felt like
a ship getting

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:43.877
hit by a tidal
wave in space.

00:00:44.378 --> 00:00:45.128
To do that...

00:00:45.128 --> 00:00:47.047
we needed the
artificial gravity

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:49.549
on Hotel Polaris
to go haywire.

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:53.971
But first,

00:00:53.971 --> 00:00:55.389
why would our
Earth orbit

00:00:55.389 --> 00:00:57.808
Hotel need
artificial gravity?

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:00.852
Well, our bodies are
used to Earth's gravity

00:01:00.852 --> 00:01:02.813
and knowing up
from down.

00:01:02.813 --> 00:01:04.439
If we go too long
without it

00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:07.609
we'll suffer some
unpleasant side effects,

00:01:07.609 --> 00:01:10.362
like, changes in blood flow,

00:01:11.113 --> 00:01:12.281
impaired vision,

00:01:13.824 --> 00:01:16.702
and big losses in our
bone and muscle mass.

00:01:16.702 --> 00:01:19.162
All to say, we don't want to
make it back from space

00:01:19.162 --> 00:01:21.373
with blurry vision
and brittle bones.

00:01:21.999 --> 00:01:25.544
So, how could we create gravity?

00:01:25.544 --> 00:01:28.213
One way to is to... well, spin.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:32.342
Rotating at high speeds
generates a force that

00:01:32.342 --> 00:01:34.761
effectively simulates
the pull of gravity.

00:01:35.262 --> 00:01:37.639
To match Earth's
gravity of 1G,

00:01:37.639 --> 00:01:40.309
a ship with a
radius of 735 feet

00:01:40.309 --> 00:01:42.311
would need to
spin at 2 RPM,

00:01:43.228 --> 00:01:45.272
but a smaller ship
one-fourth the size

00:01:45.272 --> 00:01:48.567
would need spin 4 RPM,
twice as fast.

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:49.901
The smaller the radius...

00:01:49.901 --> 00:01:51.528
the faster it's gotta spin.

00:01:51.528 --> 00:01:53.530
♪♪

00:01:55.073 --> 00:01:57.367
The space wedding
is going great,

00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:59.369
until the Hotel
takes some damage,

00:01:59.369 --> 00:02:01.079
causing it to spin faster.

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:03.540
Increasing the ships gravity

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:07.127
beyond to what humans
are used to on Earth.

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:09.796
1G increases to 2G's.

00:02:11.089 --> 00:02:14.301
That feels like
doubling your own weight...

00:02:14.593 --> 00:02:16.595
and then it
keeps spinning faster.

00:02:18.513 --> 00:02:19.806
3 G's

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:20.807
4 G's

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.311
now standing up
isn't an option

00:02:24.311 --> 00:02:25.437
and it's harder to breathe

00:02:25.437 --> 00:02:27.439
when you're pinned
down on your back.

00:02:28.315 --> 00:02:30.150
Fortunately for the guests,

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:32.778
there were some
heroes at the wedding,

00:02:32.778 --> 00:02:35.364
who slowed the spin and
saved the day.

00:02:38.575 --> 00:02:39.743
We're a little ways off from

00:02:39.743 --> 00:02:41.328
generating artificial gravity,

00:02:41.328 --> 00:02:42.579
like we see in the show.

00:02:42.913 --> 00:02:44.122
For now,

00:02:44.122 --> 00:02:46.041
astronauts complete
daily resistance

00:02:46.041 --> 00:02:48.460
training to stay
healthy in 0 G.

00:02:48.585 --> 00:02:49.753
But if we set
our sights on

00:02:49.753 --> 00:02:51.380
making a new home in space,

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:53.924
unlocking artificial
gravity can unlock

00:02:53.924 --> 00:02:56.134
new possibilities
for mankind.

00:02:56.176 --> 00:02:58.887
♪♪

